※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4561
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4561 LANG_BORROW_NOT_FROM_IT

※ The name is on the member it is written on: `⧖a` is the first member's, and
※ the second member's reference lives as long as `⧖b`, which is not what the
※ answer promised.

fn second(p: 〈&⧖a u32, &⧖b u32〉) → &⧖a u32:
    p⟦1⟧

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup, impure]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let x: u32 = 1u32
    let y: u32 = 2u32
    if second(〈&x, &y〉)⌖ = 2u32: 0u6 else: 1u6
